1	//! Experimental TypeScript 7.1 checker backend (`--experimental-semantic-types`).
2	//!
3	//! Asks TypeScript's checker for the props of each component the structural pass found, and hands
4	//! `caliper-docgen-core` a [`SemanticOutcome`] to merge (ADR 0006, ADR 0007). The checker is the `tsrs` crates, linked
5	//! in and run on a thread of their own; an explicit `tsc_path` runs that binary as a `tsc --api` process instead
6	//! (through `caliper-docgen-tsc-client`), which is how the tests and the parity gate run the Go checker. It is always
7	//! compiled in and enabled at run time. Any failure to start or finish (a missing or unpinned binary, a crash, a
8	//! timeout) yields an outcome with no components and one diagnostic, never an error: the structural result is
9	//! complete on its own.
10	//!
11	//! This slice answers function components by the exports the extractor recorded for them (a name, `default`, or the
12	//! property of an exported component a sub-component is attached to); a generic one whose first type parameter
13	//! declares a default is read at that default (`instantiate`). Class components, overloaded components and union props
14	//! types keep their structural result and say why.
15	
